sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as "Frontend<br/>(polls every 10 s)"
    participant Handler as "api::portfolio::allocations"
    participant Alloc as "AllocationsService"
    participant Portfolio as "PortfolioRepo /<br/>PortfolioDirectoryRepo"
    participant Providers as "Crypto / Equity / Fx providers<br/>(CoinMarketCap, brapi, Finnhub, BCB)"
    participant Compute as "compute_allocations<br/>(pure function)"
    participant Snap as "SnapshotRepo"

    Note over Client,Handler: PortfolioScope checks the session cookie and<br/>membership of {id} first — see docs/sequence-login.mmd.

    Client->>Handler: GET /api/portfolios/{id}/allocations
    Handler->>Alloc: current_report(id)
    Alloc->>Portfolio: fetch_positions(id)
    Portfolio-->>Alloc: Vec<WalletPosition>

    alt shared prices fresh (< PRICE_REFRESH_MINUTES) and cover every holding
        Note over Alloc: No API call — just the database
    else stale, missing a symbol, or none yet (one request at a time)
        Alloc->>Portfolio: list_all_portfolio_ids() + fetch_positions(each)
        Alloc->>Providers: crypto.fetch_quotes(held symbols) — 1 credit / 100
        Alloc->>Providers: PTAX, br/us fetch_quotes(symbols)
        Providers-->>Alloc: quotes (crypto failure → previous prices, or 502)
        loop every portfolio holding something
            Alloc->>Compute: compute_allocations(positions, quotes, targets)
            Alloc->>Snap: record_snapshot(report)
        end
    end

    Alloc->>Compute: compute_allocations(positions, shared quotes, BARCA targets)
    Compute-->>Alloc: AllocationReport
    Alloc-->>Handler: PricedReport (report + usd_brl + prices_as_of)
    Handler-->>Client: 200 OK (JSON)

    Note over Client,Snap: Every log line carries the request span<br/>(method, uri) from tower-http's TraceLayer.
